Welcome to Alpine-NTFS!

Alpine Linux running directly off an NTFS partition.
No intermediate loop mounts or rootfs images—just standard initramfs and NTFS.

How it works:
1) Kernel boots /init from the custom initramfs.
2) /init loads storage drivers and mounts the NTFS partition via FUSE (ntfs-3g).
3) The root directory is bind-mounted and handed off via switch_root.
4) Done! The whole system runs directly on NTFS.

You can install it to a disk using our patched setup-alpine script,
though using this on a daily-driver production machine is definitely not recommended.

Have fun!